  "note": "Election of the whole council (12 seats at large) on 21 May 1952; 13 candidates were nominated, but the withdrawal of Mr. G. M. Nevin left 12 for 12 seats, so all were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 9 May 1952, p. 5). The twelve named here are the nomination list minus the withdrawn candidate. Returned unopposed."
